[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   Step 108 -- full-population aphelion dipole (CometEls census).
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   The aphelion-dipole channel (step_061) measured the m=1 lean of
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   comet aphelia toward the boundary axis on four quality-selected
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   samples: the Warsaw spike, CODE class-1 matched and CODE-only,
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   and the one-apparition cohort.  Every one of those samples is a
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   catalogue elite: comets that earned full three-leg solutions.
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   A referee can therefore ask whether the dipole is a property of
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   the discovered near-parabolic population or a selection of the
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   solution-quality cut.
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   This step runs the identical tide-aware dipole test on the full
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   MPC CometEls census -- every catalogued comet with published
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   elements, quality cut or not -- restricted to the near-parabolic
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   population:
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   broad census   e in [0.90, 1.02)              (~270 comets)
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   spike proxy    e < 1 and a_osc = q/(1-e) > 250 AU
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   T1  tide calibration (|b_gal| vs isotropic, as in step_061).
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   T2  d_par = <aph . axis> under the identical tide-aware null
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   (preserve |b_gal|, uniform galactic longitude, random
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   hemisphere) on both TNO axes, the anti-axis, and the
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   galactic-pole control.
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   T3  eccentricity gradient: d_par in e-bins -- does the lean
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   strengthen toward the spike?
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   T4  membership split: comets absent from the 229-comet training
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   set carry the genuinely new information; the shared subset
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   is a same-record check.
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   T5  free dipole recovery: the census's own spherical-mean
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   aphelion direction and its separation from the measured
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   axis -- does the broad population self-organize toward the
[2026-10-16 13:42:17 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108]   axis without being told where it is?
