[2026-10-16 13:42:26 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108] verdict: On the full CometEls near-parabolic census (n=270), the aphelia lean toward the cap-declaration axis at d_par=+0.101 under the identical tide-aware null (p=0.00155); the spike-proxy subset (n=118) leans at +0.170 (p=0.0003).  The 208 comets absent from the 229-comet training set -- the genuinely new information -- lean at +0.067 (p=0.0393).  The census's own free dipole recovers (34,-37), 24 deg from the cap axis and 156 deg from the anti-axis -- the broadest discovered population self-organizes toward the measured sector without being told where it is.
